t_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"Use \\(\\neg\\neg p=p\\) and \\(\\neg\\neg\\neg p=\\neg p\\). Write \\(T,F\\) for true and false.\n\n- **(A):** Its second main conjunct simplifies to\n  \\[\n  [\\neg(\\neg T\\land F)\\land(\\neg T\\land F)]\n  \\;\\lor\\;\n  \\neg[\\neg(\\neg F\\land T)\\lor(T\\lor\\neg F)]\n  =F\\lor F=F.\n  \\]\n  Here the numerical tests, in order, are \\(6>6,\\ 39>28,\\ 100\\le2,\\ 19\\le4,\\ 48>12,\\ 4\\le2\\), and Kabul is Afghanistan’s capital. Thus **(A) is false**.\n\n- **(B):** It has the conjunct “The capital of Armenia is Gyumri,” which is false—Armenia’s capital is Yerevan. Thus **(B) is false**.\n\n- **(C):** Let \\(X\\) denote the complicated subexpression immediately conjoined with `False`. The expression reduces to\n  \\[\n  \\neg\\bigl(((X\\land F)\\lor\\neg T)\\lor\\neg(-21\\le-10)\\bigr)\n  \\land\\left(9+\\frac59>-5\\right).\n  \\]\n  Since \\(X\\land F=F\\), \\(-21\\le-10\\) is true, and \\(9+\\frac59>-5\\) is true, this is\n  \\[\n  \\neg((F\\lor F)\\lor F)\\land T=T.\n  \\]\n\n- **(D):** Its final conjunct is \\(5-\\frac92\\le-10\\), i.e. \\(\\frac12\\le-10\\), false.\n\n- **(E):** Its final conjunct is \\(5(-7)+4(2)>-8(-3)\\), i.e. \\(-27>24\\), false.\n\nFinal answer: **(C)**."}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"24h","reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","store":false,"temperature":1,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"total_tokens":0},"web_search":{"num_requests":0}},"tools":[],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":0.98,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":1408,"